# Copy to hooks/gate-guard.conf (next to gate-guard.sh) to teach the guard about MORE
# commands that count as a "gate" — a test run, typecheck, or build check whose exit code
# should decide what happens next. One command per line, added ON TOP of the built-in
# default (vitest, playwright, tsc, npm test, npm run test, npm run typecheck) — you don't
# need to repeat those here.
#
# Each line is the literal words of the invocation (an optional leading `npx` is always
# tolerated, so you don't need to list both forms). Blank lines and lines starting with #
# are ignored.
#
# No file at all: the built-in default alone applies — the safe default for a project that
# only uses the tools already covered.
pytest
jest
go test
cargo test
